<title>FRANCE: French consumer prices fell 0.1-0.2 pct in Nov.</title>
<headline>French consumer prices fell 0.1-0.2 pct in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following provisional data:</p>
<p>				    Nov	  Oct	Nov 1995</p>
<p> Month-on-month inflation -0.1-0.2     0.3	  0.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year inflation    1.5-1.6     1.8	  1.9</p>
<p> CPI Index (base 1990) 114.1-114.2   114.3	112.4</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following breakdown of the consumer price index for all households in mainland France, base 1990.</p>
<p>     Category		  Weight(pct) index  1-mo   3-mo  yr/yr</p>
<p> Food excluding tobacco	 20.17    107.1   0.5    0.8    1.2</p>
<p> Private-sector manufactures  33.05    108.5  -0.6    0.2    0.2</p>
<p> Private-sector services	19.76    125.1   0.1   -0.2    2.0</p>
<p> Energy				8.25    114.5   0.4    3.3    6.7</p>
<p> Public services ex energy     6.58    126.2  -0.3   -0.6    1.1</p>
<p> Rent, water			 6.55    129.5   0.1    0.3    2.3</p>
<p> Health spending		   5.64    110.1   0.0    0.1    0.9</p>
<p> Total excluding tobacco	98.06    113.3  -0.1    0.4    1.5</p>
<p>Cumulative inflation in the first 11 months of 1996 was 1.4-1.5 pct, INSEE said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom 33+1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
